meta {
  name: Get Student performance metrics
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/dashboard/student-performance
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

vars:pre-request {
  baseUrl: http://localhost:3000
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  # Get Student Performance Metrics
  
  Returns chart-ready metrics for the Student Performance dashboard tab. Each field in the response is either a `Dataset` (chart object) or a `LineData` (key-value list), ready for direct consumption by the frontend charting library.
  
  > **⚠️ WIP:** `c_testScores`, `c_dropoutTrend`, and `c_risk` currently return hardcoded placeholder data. `c_graduationRate` and `c_attendanceTrend` are live from the database.
  
  ## Authorization
  Requires authentication (`authenticate()`) and `"read"` permission (`authorize("read")`).
  
  ## Request
  No path parameters, query parameters, or request body.
  
  ## Response Types
  
  Every chart field conforms to one of two types defined in `types/dashboard.d.ts`:
  
  ### `Dataset`
  ```typescript
  {
    type: "bar" | "line" | "doughnut" | "pie",
    labels: object,       // array of axis labels (string[])
    datasets: object      // array of { label?: string, data: number[] }
  }
  ```
  
  ### `LineData`
  ```typescript
  Array<{ title: string, amount: number }>
  ```
  
  ---
  
  ## Success Response — `200 OK`
  
  ```json
  {
    "success": true,
    "message": "Student Performance data found successfully",
    "data": {
      "c_graduationRate": Dataset,
      "c_attendanceTrend": Dataset,
      "c_testScores": Dataset,
      "c_dropoutTrend": Dataset,
      "c_risk": Dataset
    }
  }
  ```
  
  ---
  
  ### `c_graduationRate` — `Dataset` (bar)
  
  Graduation vs dropout counts per academic year, queried from `ashExit`.
  
  | Field    | Value                                                             |
  |----------|-------------------------------------------------------------------|
  | type     | `"bar"`                                                           |
  | labels   | Shortened academic years, e.g. `["25/26", "26/27", ...]`         |
  | datasets | Two series: `"Graduated"` (COMPLETED/GRADUATED) and `"Dropped out"` (DROPPED OUT). Values are `countDistinct(ashExit.studentId)` grouped by computed academic year. |
  
  ### `c_attendanceTrend` — `Dataset` (line)
  
  Monthly total attendance for the current calendar year, queried from `ashWeeklyAttendance`.
  
  | Field    | Value                                                                         |
  |----------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
  | type     | `"line"`                                                                      |
  | labels   | `["Jan", "Feb", ..., "Dec"]`                                                  |
  | datasets | Single series `"Avg attendance"` — `SUM(cardinality(studentsInAttendance))` per month. Months with no sessions default to `0`. |
  
  ### `c_testScores` — `Dataset` (line) ⚠️ Hardcoded
  
  | Field    | Value                                                      |
  |----------|--------------------------------------------------------------|
  | type     | `"line"`                                                     |
  | labels   | `["Term 1", "Term 2", "Term 3"]`                             |
  | datasets | Three series: `"Pre-test"`, `"Mid-test"`, `"Post-test"`.     |
  
  ### `c_dropoutTrend` — `Dataset` (bar) ⚠️ Hardcoded
  
  | Field    | Value                                           |
  |----------|-------------------------------------------------|
  | type     | `"bar"`                                          |
  | labels   | `["Jan", "Feb", ..., "Dec"]`                     |
  | datasets | Single series `"Dropouts"` — monthly counts.     |
  
  ### `c_risk` — `Dataset` (doughnut) ⚠️ Hardcoded
  
  | Field    | Value                                                  |
  |----------|--------------------------------------------------------|
  | type     | `"doughnut"`                                            |
  | labels   | `["Low-risk", "At-risk"]`                               |
  | datasets | Single unlabelled series with two numeric values.       |
  
  ## Error Responses
  
  | Status | Description |
  |--------|-------------|
  | `401 Unauthorized` | Missing or invalid access token / refresh token. |
  | `403 Forbidden` | User lacks the `"read"` permission. |
  | `500 Internal Server Error` | Unexpected server error. |
}
